Not sure what to say. Graham makes a good point ... if you have simple
models and that is all you need, SQL is probably a good choice. Lots
of companies need to have their predictive models executing in real-
time, in which the score or result influences business decisions in
CRM, fraud detection, risk analysis, insurance, gaming ... Having a
scoring system that can support that, is scalable, and allows for fast
deployment of different predictive strategies is a need in many
industries.

Regards,

Alex

